THOUGHT: The NullAway error occurs because `isLogConfigurationMessage` accepts a `@Nullable Throwable ex` and then dereferences it without a null check. The recursive call with `ex.getCause()` can also pass null. I should add an early `if (ex == null) return false;` at the top of the method, which will satisfy NullAway without changing behavior (a null exception clearly cannot contain a log configuration message). After that, I need to run the targeted Gradle compile to confirm the error count drops by one and no new errors appear.

```bash
cd /home/vscode/nullness-benchmarks/spring-boot && sed -i '89,96s/private boolean isLogConfigurationMessage(@Nullable Throwable ex) {
			if (ex instanceof InvocationTargetException) {
				return isLogConfigurationMessage(ex.getCause());
			}
			String message = ex.getMessage();/private boolean isLogConfigurationMessage(@Nullable Throwable ex) {
			if (ex == null) {
				return false;
			}
			if (ex instanceof InvocationTargetException) {
				return isLogConfigurationMessage(ex.getCause());
			}
			String message = ex.getMessage();/' spring-boot-project/spring-boot/src/main/java/org/springframework/boot/SpringBootExceptionHandler.java && ./gradlew :spring-boot-project:spring-boot:compileJava -x test -q > new_build_output.log 2>&1 && grep -E "NullAway: .*errors" -n new_build_output.log || sed -n '80,110p' spring-boot-project/spring-boot/src/main/java/org/springframework/boot/SpringBootExceptionHandler.java
```

